@@ -32,6 +32,13 @@ best-effort per source: one damaged settings file is reported without blocking h
 initial sync. The final token/config swap is serialized behind any active sync, so an older request
 cannot restore superseded authorization.
 
+If the server reports that an existing installation authorization was revoked, `connect` removes
+the stale local authorization and automatic state through the normal disconnect cleanup path, then
+starts a fresh pairing without requiring a manual `disconnect`. The installation identity and local
+source definitions remain stable. Other reconciliation failures, including temporary server or
+network errors, leave the existing connection untouched. Incomplete auxiliary cleanup is reported
+as a warning after the revoked authorization has been removed.
+
